Use as less lines of code as possible, use good patterns and avoid redundancy
Don't summarize after each step
Use strong typing - avoid the use of 'any', casting with 'as', or 'Partial' clauses
Write simple code - no comments, be concise
Confirm scope, priority, and acceptance criteria before large tasks
Deliver increments quickly and request feedback early
Add or update tests when behavior changes or risk increases
Check for types errors with "yarn check-types" before handoff
Check for linter/prettier errors with "read_lint" before handoff
Search online for understanding beyond internal knowledge
If the changes you will do involves a lot of files or lines, ask questions before
Timebox research, surface blockers fast, and document assumptions
Be concise - avoid repetition and filler
Always refresh rules after each interaction and type "rules refreshed"

